# Dynamic array keeps heterogeneous element identities

Verifies insertion and indexed replacement accept unrelated values, including
nested arrays and null, while a numeric-looking string remains a string.

>>> source
let values = [1, "2", 3]
values->push("hello")
values->unshift(true)
values->push(null)
values->push([4, 5])
values[1] = "changed"
print(values[2] + "x")
print(values)

<<< stdout
2x
[true, changed, 2, 3, hello, null, [4, 5]]

<<< stderr
